# Phase 3 — Workflows and Orchestration (Weeks 4–5)

## Prompt 7 — Workflow creation with DAG validation

> **Read first:** `docs/Architecture.md` §10.3, §14.1 (Workflow, WorkflowAgent), §15.5 (Workflow.status), §3 (P10 — the DAG is validated at creation, not at execution) · `docs/FRS .md` §3.3 (WFL, FR-WFL-001…009), §5 (BR-06) · `docs/PRD .md` (US-02)
>
> Implement the workflow endpoints in `backend/app/api/workflows.py`: `POST /api/workflows` (**FR-WFL-001**), `GET /api/workflows` and `GET /api/workflows/{id}` (**FR-WFL-007**) — the detail response returns the DAG structure React Flow consumes directly.
>
> Validation at creation time only:
> - **FR-WFL-002** — a topological sort; reject with `400 WORKFLOW_CYCLE_DETECTED` if the dependencies aren't a valid DAG
> - **FR-WFL-003** — reject a step referencing an unknown `agent_id` at creation, not at run time
> - **FR-WFL-004** — the topological sort runs **once**, and the result is stored on `WorkflowAgent.step_order`; the Orchestrator must never re-sort at run time
> - **FR-WFL-005** — `WorkflowAgent.input_mapping` declares which upstream output field feeds this step
> - **FR-WFL-006** — `DRAFT → ACTIVE → ARCHIVED` per Architecture §15.5; `ACTIVE` only after validation passes
>
> Support 1–5 agents per workflow (**FR-WFL-009**).
>
> **Done when:** US-02 passes — a cyclic definition is rejected before saving, and a valid workflow stores a fixed `step_order`.

## Prompt 8 — Orchestrator: sequential DAG execution

> **Read first:** `docs/Architecture.md` §11 (Layer 3 — Orchestration, especially §11.2 scheduler algorithm), §15.1 and §15.3 (state machines), §3 (P2, P3, P13, P14) · `docs/FRS .md` §3.4 (ORC, FR-ORC-001…014), §5 (BR-13) · `docs/PRD .md` (US-04)
>
> Write `backend/orchestrator/orchestrator.py` and `backend/orchestrator/step_executor.py`, following Architecture §11.2's scheduler algorithm and §11.1's one-responsibility-per-file split.
>
> - **FR-ORC-001** — `POST /api/workflows/{id}/executions` returns `execution_id` immediately; the run proceeds via FastAPI `BackgroundTasks`. The API layer never blocks (Architecture P2).
> - **FR-ORC-002** — `Orchestrator.run_execution(execution_id: UUID) -> None`
> - **FR-ORC-003 / FR-ORC-004** — steps run in the stored `step_order`; sibling steps with no dependency between them run under `asyncio.gather`
> - **FR-ORC-005** — step N's input includes the declared upstream output field(s) (US-04: no manual wiring)
> - **FR-ORC-012** — `StepExecutor.run_step(step_id: UUID) -> dict`
> - **FR-ORC-008 / FR-ORC-009** — the 5-state machine, enforced through the `can_transition` function from Prompt 2
> - **FR-ORC-010** — `Execution.status` rolls up per Architecture §15.3
> - **FR-ORC-013** — status and checkpoint written in the same SQLAlchemy transaction
>
> Implement **FR-ORC-011**'s `recovery_stage` field now (values per Architecture §15.2) even though nothing sets it beyond `NONE` yet.
>
> Critically, implement **FR-ADP-005 / FR-DIAG-002 / BR-13** inside `step_executor.py`: every exception and every structured agent error is normalised to `{"status": "FAILED", "error_type": "...", "raw_error": "..."}` before anything downstream sees it.
>
> **Done when:** a 2-agent workflow runs end to end in declared order, and orchestration bookkeeping stays under the 300 ms/step budget in **FR-ORC-014**.
